KubeOS: this directory is a mountpoint.

/opt/local-path-provisioner is where local-path-provisioner (the default
StorageClass) keeps every PersistentVolume it hands out. On KubeOS it is NOT part
of the root filesystem: first boot creates the thin LVM pool kubeos-vg/kubeos-data,
formats the thin volume kubeos-vg/pod-data with XFS and mounts it here (see
/usr/bin/kubeos-storage-init and /etc/fstab), so workload data never fills /.

This placeholder file exists only so the directory is present in the image even if
first boot has not run yet. Once the pool is mounted it is hidden behind the
mount. Check where you actually are with:

    findmnt /opt/local-path-provisioner

If that prints nothing, the mount is gone and anything written here is going to
the root filesystem - fix that with `mount /opt/local-path-provisioner` and read
`journalctl -u node-setup -b`.
